This appears to be from a CBP ruling on Bug-A-Salt, which classified the items as toy guns. The likely heading is 9503.00, toys. Within it, subheading 9503.00.00 has the statistical suffixes 9503.00.0073 ("Other toys; ... Other") and 9503.00.0071 (Toys... for ages?). The older structure (before 2022) was 9503.00.00 with suffixes: 9503.00.0073 "Other toys and models, not elsewhere specified." Under the 2022 revision, the new 9503.00.00 breakdown has 9503.00.0073 for "Other".

Alternatively, the rulings might have treated the items as spring-powered air guns under 9304.00.. But the description says they "do not provide the power or function of common air guns," which points to a toy. The CO2 cartridge on the SHRED-ER might have raised the air gun question, but the stated conclusion is toy. I settled on 9503.00.0073 for "other toys".

{"hts_code": "9503.00.0073", "reason": "The plastic Bug-A-Salt salt-blasting guns are toy guns that lack the power or function of true air guns (heading 9304), so they are classified as other toys in heading 9503."}
